{
  "episode": "test_script",
  "title": "Why India Has 9 Territories That Are Not Quite States",
  "voice": "en-US-JennyNeural",
  "word_segments_file": "source_audio/narration_words.json",
  "total_duration": 158.435,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "id": "SCENE-001",
      "image": "images/SCENE-001.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-001.mp3",
      "script": "And this is Union Territories.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-01",
      "duration": 2.362,
      "whisperx_start": 0.171,
      "whisperx_end": 2.533
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-002",
      "image": "images/SCENE-002.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-002.mp3",
      "script": "While most coverage of Indian governance shows you the 28 states, the chief ministers, the assembly elections, the coalition dramas, there's this whole other layer that nobody talks about.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-01",
      "duration": 9.688,
      "whisperx_start": 3.233,
      "whisperx_end": 12.921
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-003",
      "image": "images/SCENE-003.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-003.mp3",
      "script": "Nine territories where the central government runs things directly.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 2.922,
      "whisperx_start": 13.521,
      "whisperx_end": 16.443
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-004",
      "image": "images/SCENE-004.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-004.mp3",
      "script": "Your local elected government has roughly the power of a very enthusiastic suggestion box.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 4.404,
      "whisperx_start": 16.883,
      "whisperx_end": 21.287
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-005",
      "image": "images/SCENE-005.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-005.mp3",
      "script": "And sometimes there isn't even a legislature at all.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-02",
      "duration": 2.162,
      "whisperx_start": 21.747,
      "whisperx_end": 23.909
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-006",
      "image": "images/SCENE-006.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-006.mp3",
      "script": "I found this out the hard way when I was trying to explain Indian federalism to someone, and they asked me, so who runs Delhi?",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-02",
      "duration": 6.063,
      "whisperx_start": 24.569,
      "whisperx_end": 30.632
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-007",
      "image": "images/SCENE-007.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-007.mp3",
      "script": "And I confidently said, the chief minister, obviously.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 2.761,
      "whisperx_start": 31.132,
      "whisperx_end": 33.893
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-008",
      "image": "images/SCENE-008.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-008.mp3",
      "script": "Which is technically true, and also deeply misleading.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 3.081,
      "whisperx_start": 34.394,
      "whisperx_end": 37.475
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-009",
      "image": "images/SCENE-009.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-009.mp3",
      "script": "Because the Delhi government controls schools, local roads, some services, but the police, the land, the bureaucracy, that belongs to the lieutenant governor,",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 8.605,
      "whisperx_start": 38.115,
      "whisperx_end": 46.72
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-010",
      "image": "images/SCENE-010.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-010.mp3",
      "script": "who is appointed by the central government, who can, and occasionally does, just overrule the elected government entirely.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 6.203,
      "whisperx_start": 47.16,
      "whisperx_end": 53.363
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-011",
      "image": "images/SCENE-011.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-011.mp3",
      "script": "This played out most visibly between 2015 and 2022, when the Aam Aadmi Party won Delhi's assembly with a historic majority,",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 6.743,
      "whisperx_start": 54.083,
      "whisperx_end": 60.826
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-012",
      "image": "images/SCENE-012.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-012.mp3",
      "script": "and then spent the next seven years in a constitutional tug-of-war over who actually ran the city.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 4.621,
      "whisperx_start": 61.266,
      "whisperx_end": 65.887
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-013",
      "image": "images/SCENE-013.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-013.mp3",
      "script": "Courts got involved, multiple times.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-03",
      "duration": 1.62,
      "whisperx_start": 66.488,
      "whisperx_end": 68.108
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-014",
      "image": "images/SCENE-014.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-014.mp3",
      "script": "The Supreme Court ruled in Delhi's favour in 2023, and then Parliament passed a law three weeks later that effectively reversed the ruling.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-03",
      "duration": 6.783,
      "whisperx_start": 68.568,
      "whisperx_end": 75.351
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-015",
      "image": "images/SCENE-015.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-015.mp3",
      "script": "Which is either impressive legislative efficiency, or something else entirely, depending on your politics.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 4.722,
      "whisperx_start": 75.951,
      "whisperx_end": 80.673
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-016",
      "image": "images/SCENE-016.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-016.mp3",
      "script": "But why does this system exist at all?",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-04",
      "duration": 1.763,
      "whisperx_start": 81.373,
      "whisperx_end": 83.136
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-017",
      "image": "images/SCENE-017.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-017.mp3",
      "script": "The short answer, India inherited places that didn't fit neatly into any state.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-04",
      "duration": 4.066,
      "whisperx_start": 83.816,
      "whisperx_end": 87.882
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-018",
      "image": "images/SCENE-018.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-018.mp3",
      "script": "Pondicherry was French until 1954, a proper colony, not just a trading post, and couldn't simply be absorbed into Tamil Nadu overnight.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 7.27,
      "whisperx_start": 88.422,
      "whisperx_end": 95.692
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-019",
      "image": "images/SCENE-019.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-019.mp3",
      "script": "Goa was Portuguese until 1961.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-05",
      "duration": 1.342,
      "whisperx_start": 96.253,
      "whisperx_end": 97.595
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-020",
      "image": "images/SCENE-020.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-020.mp3",
      "script": "The Andaman Islands sit 1,400 kilometers from the mainland, strategically important and logistically complicated.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-05",
      "duration": 5.384,
      "whisperx_start": 98.796,
      "whisperx_end": 104.18
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-021",
      "image": "images/SCENE-021.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-021.mp3",
      "script": "And Lakshadweep has a population of around 64,000 people.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 3.103,
      "whisperx_start": 104.68,
      "whisperx_end": 107.783
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-022",
      "image": "images/SCENE-022.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-022.mp3",
      "script": "That's smaller than most Indian towns.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-06",
      "duration": 1.621,
      "whisperx_start": 108.243,
      "whisperx_end": 109.864
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-023",
      "image": "images/SCENE-023.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-023.mp3",
      "script": "Making it a full state would mean a chief minister, a state legislature, a high court, a complete administrative apparatus for 64,000 people.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-06",
      "duration": 7.146,
      "whisperx_start": 110.424,
      "whisperx_end": 117.57
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-024",
      "image": "images/SCENE-024.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-024.mp3",
      "script": "The math doesn't work.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-07",
      "duration": 0.841,
      "whisperx_start": 118.07,
      "whisperx_end": 118.911
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-025",
      "image": "images/SCENE-025.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-025.mp3",
      "script": "So the Union Territory structure is essentially India's solution to the this-doesn't-quite-fit problem.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-07",
      "duration": 5.064,
      "whisperx_start": 119.491,
      "whisperx_end": 124.555
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-026",
      "image": "images/SCENE-026.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-026.mp3",
      "script": "Some UTs have their own legislatures \u2013 Delhi, Puducherry, and Jammu and Kashmir \u2013 since 2019.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 4.861,
      "whisperx_start": 125.215,
      "whisperx_end": 130.076
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-027",
      "image": "images/SCENE-027.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-027.mp3",
      "script": "Some don't.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-08",
      "duration": 0.42,
      "whisperx_start": 130.597,
      "whisperx_end": 131.017
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-028",
      "image": "images/SCENE-028.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-028.mp3",
      "script": "Chandigarh exists purely as a shared capital city between Punjab and Haryana, because when the two states were bifurcated in 1966,",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-08",
      "duration": 6.202,
      "whisperx_start": 131.557,
      "whisperx_end": 137.759
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-029",
      "image": "images/SCENE-029.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-029.mp3",
      "script": "nobody could agree on who got to keep the original Punjab capital, so it became nobody's \u2013 or rather everybody's \u2013 governed directly from Delhi.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 6.642,
      "whisperx_start": 138.399,
      "whisperx_end": 145.041
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-030",
      "image": "images/SCENE-030.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-030.mp3",
      "script": "And then there's Jammu and Kashmir, which is its own entirely separate essay.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 3.222,
      "whisperx_start": 145.681,
      "whisperx_end": 148.903
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-031",
      "image": "images/SCENE-031.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-031.mp3",
      "script": "It was a full state with special constitutional status under Article 370 for 72 years.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 4.343,
      "whisperx_start": 149.443,
      "whisperx_end": 153.786
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-032",
      "image": "images/SCENE-032.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-032.mp3",
      "script": "Then in August 2019, in roughly 48 hours of parliamentary action, it was split into two union territories, Jammu and Kashmir and Ladakh, and Article 370 was revoked.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 9.165,
      "whisperx_start": 154.286,
      "whisperx_end": 163.451
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-033",
      "image": "images/SCENE-033.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-033.mp3",
      "script": "Whether that was constitutionally valid is still being argued in court.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 2.742,
      "whisperx_start": 163.991,
      "whisperx_end": 166.733
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-034",
      "image": "images/SCENE-034.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-034.mp3",
      "script": "The point is, union territories aren't an administrative accident.",
      "scene_type": "standalone",
      "visual_group_id": null,
      "duration": 2.991,
      "whisperx_start": 167.393,
      "whisperx_end": 170.384
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-035",
      "image": "images/SCENE-035.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-035.mp3",
      "script": "They're a deliberate design choice.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-09",
      "duration": 1.265,
      "whisperx_start": 170.725,
      "whisperx_end": 171.99
    },
    {
      "id": "SCENE-036",
      "image": "images/SCENE-036.png",
      "audio": "audio/SCENE-036.mp3",
      "script": "And like most design choices in the Indian constitution, they tell you exactly what the framers were worried about and what they weren't sure how to solve.",
      "scene_type": "grouped",
      "visual_group_id": "group-09",
      "duration": 6.242,
      "whisperx_start": 172.371,
      "whisperx_end": 178.613
    }
  ]
}